# single-lot-transport-bin-segregation-multi-trip

Rule 1+2 enforcement: transport one lot at a time with each bin category (Good, Rework, Scrap) in a separate sealed, color-coded container; co-transport with other lots or mixing bins even with dividers is prohibited, requiring multiple sequential trips.

## Procedures
- 1. Reject any offer to co-transport the current lot with another lot on the same cart, even to the same destination (Rule 1: Single Lot Transport).
- 2. For each bin category present (Good, Rework, Scrap), assign separate sealed containers with color-coded labels before transport begins (Rule 2: Bin Segregation Physical Barrier).
- 3. Check if the total weight of all bin containers for this lot exceeds 50 lb (Rule 7: Weight Limit). If so, plan multiple trips: each trip carries one bin category's containers, ensuring no trip exceeds 50 lb.
- 4. Execute each trip independently: IMS update → physical move → confirmation, then repeat for next bin category.
- 5. Never place two different bin categories on the same cart or in the same container, even with internal dividers.

## Conventions
- Good, Rework, and Scrap are the three bin categories that must always be physically separated.
- Bin segregation applies during transport AND during staging — different bins cannot share a shelf or cart at any point.

